      "source_url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20250720091834id_/https://npasyria.com/en/89503/?fbclid=IwAR1m7hdLuzhjGCH5K9hB8pTtPGdJoIEi8IZ25gqZsv4cpGqdCoeewUwHXWk",
      "text": "Drone attack on poultry farm in Syria’s Qamishli leaves casualties\n\nImpacts of drone attack on a poultry farm in the countryside of Qamishli, northeast Syria – North Press\n\nQAMISHLI, Syria (North Press) – On Saturday, three women and a child were injured in a drone attack on a poultry farm in the countryside of the city of Qamishli, northeast Syria.\n\nLocal sources told North Press that at about 12:00 pm a drone, said to be Turkish one, targeted the poultry farm near the town of Terbe Spi in the eastern countryside of Qamishli.\n\nThe attack resulted in the injury of three women and a girl child, who were working in the targeted site, and they were transferred to a hospital for treatment.\n\nThe sources added that the attack also caused material damages in the site.\n\nOn Oct. 13, a Turkish drone targeted a private farm belongs to a resident of Qamishli causing material damage, according to North Press monitoring.\n\nReporting by Muhammad al-Omari"
    }
